### Payment Failure Tests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
@paymentId = YOUR_PAYMENT_ID_HERE

### 1. Create Order (Normal Flow)
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/create-order
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "BK123456",
  "flightId": "1",
  "flightNumber": "AI101",
  "origin": "BOM",
  "destination": "BLR",
  "travelDate": "2025-01-20T10:00:00Z",
  "passengerId": "user123",
  "passengerName": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "phone": "+919876543210",
  "seatNumber": "12A",
  "cabinClass": "Economy",
  "baseFare": 5000,
  "taxAmount": 500,
  "serviceFee": 100,
  "currency": "INR"
}

### 2. User Exits Without Payment - Mark as Failed
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments/fail
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "paymentId": "{{paymentId}}",
  "reason": "User exited without payment"
}

### 3. Check Payment Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Get All Payments (Admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/all?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Get User Payments
GET {{baseUrl}}/payments/user/user123?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Notes:
# - Payments in "Pending" or "OrderCreated" status will auto-expire after 15 minutes
# - Background service runs every 5 minutes to check for expired payments
# - Failed payments will have status "Failed" with reason "Payment expired - User did not complete payment"
# - Manual failure can be triggered using /payments/fail endpoint
